# LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working copy.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which stores LF and checks out
# CRLF. That is the right default for a mixed team and the wrong one here: the
# files are edited by tooling that writes LF, so a checkout would flip every
# line of every source file and the next write would flip them back — a diff of
# the whole project with no change in it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Built place files are binary; never try to diff or convert them.
*.rbxlx binary
*.rbxl binary
*.rbxm binary
*.rbxmx binary
